WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.672 --> 00:00:05.032
Microsoft is very interested in healthcare problems

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:08.391
because the healthcare industry has got a lot of

00:00:08.392 --> 00:00:13.024
technology, a lot of data and yet we feel that we are not

00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:15.606
making the best use of that technology and that data.

00:00:16.993 --> 00:00:20.526
Novartis approached us; they're very interested in the

00:00:20.527 --> 00:00:24.880
ability to assess and diagnose the progression of multiple

00:00:24.881 --> 00:00:28.951
sclerosis, which is a very tricky disease to try and assess.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.561
Multiple Sclerosis is a disease of the central nervous system

00:00:33.562 --> 00:00:36.902
and it can affect people’s everyday lives, so it can affect their

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:40.200
balance, their motor abilities, their ability to walk, to eat.

00:00:40.201 --> 00:00:43.253
It can also affect cognitive abilities and vision.

00:00:44.207 --> 00:00:47.881
We saw a real possibility to use all of the expertise that we

00:00:47.882 --> 00:00:49.982
have in the building around machine learning and computer

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:53.227
vision and the design of user experiences to bring all of those

00:00:53.228 --> 00:00:55.857
different disciplines together, to provide some data that's

00:00:55.858 --> 00:00:59.030
going to help the expert make a better assessment.

00:01:03.154 --> 00:01:06.887
The role of machine learning in Assess MS is to find an

00:01:06.888 --> 00:01:10.759
automated way to classify the patient's condition, given the

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.613
a certain set of movements. So the goal is simply to

00:01:13.614 --> 00:01:15.184
standardize.

00:01:15.185 --> 00:01:17.449
Multiple Sclerosis is currently assessed by a Neurologist

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.247
using a clinical standardized rating scale.

00:01:20.248 --> 00:01:22.431
So they might ask a patient to stretch out their hands

00:01:22.432 --> 00:01:26.238
touch their nose, walk for five meters. And this is

00:01:26.239 --> 00:01:28.462
where technology has a real strength.

00:01:28.866 --> 00:01:31.952
Assess MS System provides a consistent, quantified measure

00:01:31.953 --> 00:01:34.629
of motor ability over time.

00:01:35.245 --> 00:01:37.200
As the disease progresses, you can see stronger

00:01:37.201 --> 00:01:40.047
and stronger impairments on the motors skills and the machine

00:01:40.048 --> 00:01:42.545
learning basically just tries to figure out where do

00:01:42.546 --> 00:01:45.969
certain signatures start for which category

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:48.737
and how do they develop as you cross the

00:01:48.738 --> 00:01:49.738
boundary to the next category?

00:01:55.703 --> 00:01:57.981
At the moment the Assess MS project is focused around

00:01:57.982 --> 00:02:00.788
providing this consistent measure in clinical trials.

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:04.498
We worked with a team at Novartis Pharma AG

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:08.350
who helped us understand what kinds of things are needed

00:02:08.351 --> 00:02:11.435
in clinical trials and how it is that we go about partnering

00:02:11.436 --> 00:02:13.356
with clinics.

00:02:14.041 --> 00:02:16.742
It requires multiple stakeholders and what we've been

00:02:16.743 --> 00:02:20.225
able to do in this collaboration is work with university

00:02:20.226 --> 00:02:23.307
hospitals, Microsoft Research, as well as our own

00:02:23.308 --> 00:02:26.676
Novartis research teams, to bring together the best talent

00:02:26.677 --> 00:02:29.589
needed to completely change the paradigm in how we

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:33.164
assess MS patients' disability progression.

00:02:34.548 --> 00:02:36.258
We're not trying to replace the Neurologist or the

00:02:36.259 --> 00:02:38.504
Nurse. What we're trying to do instead is to very much

00:02:38.505 --> 00:02:44.485
bolster or augment the kinds of expertise that they already have. It's there to really help

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:48.840
the doctor give a consistent measurement over time to help the patient to make the best

00:02:48.846 --> 00:02:50.810
decisions they can about their treatment.

